    <h2>Quality control: three stages</h2>
    <p>
      Quality control in incense follows a three-stage process:
      <strong>incoming inspection</strong> (verifying species, grade, and adulteration when material
      arrives), <strong>in-process control</strong> (holding blend, particle size, moisture, and
      forming steady during production), and <strong>final inspection</strong> (checking the finished
      product against the agreed specification before release).
    </p>
    <p>
      The product you reorder is the <em>consistency</em>, not the individual stick. The variables
      that matter — material consistency, particle size, moisture, density, and burn behavior — are
      the same ones documented in the
      <a href="/blog/how-incense-is-made/">how incense is made</a> guide and the
      <a href="/blog/agarwood-powder-vs-chips/">form-and-use</a> references.
    </p>

